# The Waypoints tab: the places the mesh has shared, and one of them opened.
#
# The column on the right is what this scene exists for. A waypoint carries a point and nothing
# else useful about where it is, so the list answers the only two questions a handheld with no
# map can: how far away it is, and which way it lies from our own radio's fix. Both come out of
# src/geo/vector.c, and the list is ordered by the first of them - nearest first, because that
# is the order the tab is for.
#
# The places are put at nodes that are already in the demo roster, so the ranges below are
# measured between two real fixes rather than between two numbers typed to agree.

scene demo
waypoint ALFA Ridge repeater | up the fire road, gate code is on the tag
waypoint FXTR Trailhead
waypoint CHRL Water cache

tab waypoints
hold 1200

# Open the nearest one: the range and the coordinates, the note the sharer left, who shared it
# and on what channel, then the two things that can be done with it.
key a
hold 1600

# The delete row asks before it acts, because withdrawing a place takes it off the mesh for
# everybody rather than only off this Brick.
key down 12
hold 600
key a
hold 1400
key b
hold 800
